[E0202] Error: WRONG ASSIGNMENT: value assignment (`:=`) cannot target an object reference
   ╭─[ ref_with_value_assign.sim:1:42 ]
   │
 1 │ begin class P; begin end; ref(P) p; p := none; end;
   │                                          ──┬─  
   │                                            ╰─── this is a `ref` destination
   │ 
   │ Help 1: write `:-` instead of `:=`
   │ 
   │ Help 2: suggestion: replace `:=` with `:-`
   │ 
   │ Note: `:=` copies values; object references are bound with `:-` (Standard §3.6)
───╯
